# Street Cart Chicken & Yellow Rice

Based on [https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/…](https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/street-cart-chicken-and-yellow-rice) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251130122133/https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/street-cart-chicken-and-yellow-rice))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Chicken

- [ ] 4 [chicken thighs]{ ing="chicken-thighs" }, boneless (1 lb)
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, 5g (a sprinkle)
- [ ] [whole cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }, ~5
- [ ] [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" }, 5g (a spoonful)
- [ ] [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, 2g (a sprinkle)
- [ ] [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, 20 cranks (a spoonful)
- [ ] [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, 3 cloves
- [ ] [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, 1/4 lemon
- [ ] [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, 30g (2 spoonfuls)

### Yellow rice

- [ ] [basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } 200g (1 part)
- [ ] [chicken broth]{ ing="chicken-broth" } or water, 250g (1 part)
- [ ] [butter]{ ing="butter" }, unsalted, 15g (a spoonful)
- [ ] [onions]{ ing="onions" }, finely diced, 1/8
- [ ] [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" }, 5g (a spoonful)
- [ ] [turmeric powder]{ ing="turmeric-powder" }, 5g (a spoonful)
- [ ] [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, 5g (a spoonful)
- [ ] [bay leaves]{ ing="bay-leaves" }, 1-2
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, to taste

### White sauce

- [ ] [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, 100g (2 parts)
- [ ] [greek yogurt]{ ing="greek-yogurt" }, 50g (1 part)
- [ ] [white vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" }, 10g (a splash)
- [ ] [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, 1/4 lemon
- [ ] [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, 10 cranks (a sprinkle)
- [ ] [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, a sprinkle
- [ ] [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, a sprinkle
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, to taste

### Red hot sauce

- [ ] [water]{ ing="water" }, 100g, 2 parts
- [ ] [white vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" }, 50g, 1 part
- [ ] [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }, 15g, 1/3 part
- [ ] [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }, 5g, a spoonful
- [ ] [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, 1/2 lemon
- [ ] [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, 10g, a spoonful
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, to taste

### For serving

- [ ] [pita bread]{ ing="pita-bread" }
- [ ] [lettuce]{ ing="lettuce" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, diced

## Recipe

### Marinate the chicken

1. Sprinkle the [chicken thighs]{ ing="chicken-thighs" } with [salt]{ ing="salt" } and set them aside.
1. Crush the [cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" } and cumin in a mortar and pestle. Add [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } cloves into the mortar with the spices and crush into a rough paste.
1. In a large mixing bowl, combine the [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, mayo, and spice mixture. Add the [chicken thighs]{ ing="chicken-thighs" } and mix to thoroughly coat the exterior. Cover and place in the fridge to marinate for up to 24 hrs or cook right away.

### Rice

1. Melt [butter]{ ing="butter" } in a pot over medium heat.
1. Add [onion]{ ing="onions" }, cumin, turmeric, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, and bay leaf. Bloom the aromatics until fragrant but not burnt, about 30 seconds.
1. Add the rice to the pan with the aromatics and mix. Lightly toast the rice and stir for about 2 minutes.
1. Add [chicken broth]{ ing="chicken-broth" }, turn up the heat, and cover the pan to bring to a boil.
1. Reduce the heat to the lowest setting. Let the rice gently simmer while covered for about 20 minutes.
1. Meanwhile, feel free to cook the chicken or mix the sauces (next steps)
1. Uncover and taste the rice! Add [salt]{ ing="salt" } as needed or stir a little more [butter]{ ing="butter" } to make the rice more unctuous.

### Make the red sauce

1. Add all ingredients to a blender. Process until smooth.
1. Add sauce to a pot and simmer over medium-low heat to develop flavors and reduce the sauce.
1. Taste and adjust for [salt]{ ing="salt" } and [vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" } - NOTE: This will be hot.
1. Let cool before storing in a bottle in the fridge.

### Mix the white sauce

1. Place bowl over a scale, and add the mayo, [yogurt]{ ing="greek-yogurt" }, [vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } into a bowl. Mix together.
1. Taste it! Adjust [salt]{ ing="salt" } or any spice/herb additions as you see fit.

### Cook the chicken

1. When ready to cook, place a pan over medium-high heat. Once hot, sear the [chicken thighs]{ ing="chicken-thighs" } on both sides until the internal temp reaches at least 165 F.
1. Chop the chicken into pieces in the pan or let them rest, then slice.

### Assemble & serve

1. Serve a portion of chicken & rice on a plate and drizzle with both of the sauces, as desired.
1. Optional: serve with [pita bread]{ ing="pita-bread" } or fresh vegetables/herbs for garnish
